WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:16,480
and how reliable are the tumor markers? Again, there isn't any test that's perfect. Some people will

00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:22,640
ever show positive tumor markers, they'll have an extremely aggressive cancer. Some cancers don't

00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:30,160
show positive tumor markers. So, you know, they're like lung cancer, let's use that as an example,

00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:35,600
might not show positive tumor markers at all. Breast cancer typically will show positive

00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:42,240
tumor markers, but not always. You know, pancreatic cancer will typically show positive CA-199,

00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:55,600
almost always. And colon cancers will typically show positive CEA and CA-125, but not always.

00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:08,560
So, that's, that's the, again, just like anything nothing is perfect.

